<Testimonial
  title="Testimonial | Martin Boonsanoh"
  heading="Martin Boonsanoh"
  description="Martin from Berlin turned 27 the week he ordained alongside 40 monks from many countries, after months of overwork left him unhappy."
  detail="11th European Ordination Program participant"
  portrait={img2026073}
  portraitAlt="Portrait of Martin Boonsanoh"
>
  <p>
    I’m Martin from Berlin, Germany. This week I turn 27, and it feels especially meaningful because I am ordaining
    together with 40 monks from many different countries. It is the first time we have been so many, and that makes this
    moment very special.
  </p>
  <p>
    The ordination day itself was unforgettable. People from all over came to support us, and I feel deeply thankful to
    everyone who was part of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before I joined this program, the last three months had been very stressful. I was working too much, chasing money
    and trying to please everyone, and nothing really made me happy. Since arriving here I meditate every day with the
    monks. Their teaching and the practice have helped me gain more control over myself, more inner peace, more
    happiness, and greater mindfulness.
  </p>
